From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000087 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 22:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] watchdog: mtk: prioritize MT6797 TOPRGU restart

The arm64 PSCI restart notifier runs at priority 129, while the MediaTek
watchdog restart handler uses the watchdog-core default priority 128.  An
attempted normal reboot on the Gemini PDA appeared to hang, although its
internal failure stage was not captured.  The same hardware subsequently
reset through the MT6797 TOPRGU watchdog expiry path, and the working 3.18
kernel directs MT6797 restart through TOPRGU rather than PSCI.

If the higher-priority PSCI call does not reset or return, the restart
notifier chain cannot reach the existing TOPRGU software-reset callback.
Make restart priority platform data and select priority 255 for MT6797,
which the watchdog core defines as preempting all other restart handlers.
Retain priority 128 for every other MediaTek watchdog variant.

This changes only immediate restart-handler ordering.  It leaves PSCI CPU
operations, watchdog timeout behavior, Device Tree, and configuration
unchanged.  Hardware validation of the immediate TOPRGU restart remains a
separate gate.
---
 drivers/watchdog/mtk_wdt.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/watchdog/mtk_wdt.c b/drivers/watchdog/mtk_wdt.c
--- a/drivers/watchdog/mtk_wdt.c
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/mtk_wdt.c
@@ -84,6 +84,7 @@ struct mtk_wdt_data {
 	int toprgu_sw_rst_num;
 	bool has_swsysrst_en;
 	bool use_auto_restart;
+	unsigned int restart_priority;
 };
 
 static const struct mtk_wdt_data mt2712_data = {
@@ -100,6 +101,7 @@ static const struct mtk_wdt_data mt6795_data = {
 
 static const struct mtk_wdt_data mt6797_data = {
 	.use_auto_restart = true,
+	.restart_priority = 255,
 };
 
 static const struct mtk_wdt_data mt7986_data = {
@@ -460,7 +462,9 @@ static int mtk_wdt_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	watchdog_init_timeout(&mtk_wdt->wdt_dev, timeout, dev);
 	watchdog_set_nowayout(&mtk_wdt->wdt_dev, nowayout);
-	watchdog_set_restart_priority(&mtk_wdt->wdt_dev, 128);
+	watchdog_set_restart_priority(&mtk_wdt->wdt_dev,
+				      wdt_data && wdt_data->restart_priority ?
+				      wdt_data->restart_priority : 128);
 
 	watchdog_set_drvdata(&mtk_wdt->wdt_dev, mtk_wdt);
 
